the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    the calculation date is *a date*; scenario element.
    the irregular income quarter cap is *an amount*.
    the irregular income excluded from snap income of *a household* is *an amount*.
    the student child income age limit is *a number*.
    the student child earned income excluded from snap income of *a person* is *an amount*.
    the income of *a household* received too infrequently or irregularly to be reasonably anticipated; scenario element.
    the irregular income amount in certification period of *a household* is *an amount*; scenario element.
    *a person* is child member of household; scenario element.
    *a person* is elementary or secondary school student; scenario element.
    the person age of *a person* is *a number*; scenario element.
    the child earned income amount of *a person* is *an amount*; scenario element.

the knowledge base us_statutes_7_2014_d includes:


% 7 U.S.C. 2014(d) — us:statutes/7/2014/d
the text of "7 USC 2014(d)(2)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2014/d.yaml".

the text of "7 USC 2014(d)(7)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2014/d.yaml".

the irregular income quarter cap is 30 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D.

rule irregular_income_excluded_from_snap_income with provenance "7 USC 2014(d)(2)":
the irregular income excluded from snap income of a household is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the income of the household received too infrequently or irregularly to be reasonably anticipated
        and the irregular income amount in certification period of the household is an amount M
        and the irregular income quarter cap is an amount K
        and the minimum of M and K is N
        otherwise the household is a household
        and N = 0.

the student child income age limit is 17 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D.

rule student_child_earned_income_excluded_from_snap_income with provenance "7 USC 2014(d)(7)":
the student child earned income excluded from snap income of a person is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is child member of household
        and the person is elementary or secondary school student
        and the person age of the person is a number M
        and the student child income age limit is a number K
        and M <= K
        and the child earned income amount of the person is N
        otherwise the person is a person
        and N = 0.

scenario irregular_income_exclusion_caps_at_quarter_limit is, as stated in "sources/us/statutes/7/2014/d.test.yaml" at case 1:
    household_1 is a household.
    the calculation date is 2026-01-01.
    the income of household_1 received too infrequently or irregularly to be reasonably anticipated.
    the irregular income amount in certification period of household_1 is 45.
    q_irregular_income_excluded_from_snap_income expects answers ["the irregular income excluded from snap income of household_1 is 30"].
    q_irregular_income_quarter_cap expects answers ["the irregular income quarter cap is 30"].

scenario irregular_income_not_excluded_without_irregularity_condition is, as stated in "sources/us/statutes/7/2014/d.test.yaml" at case 2:
    household_1 is a household.
    the calculation date is 2026-01-01.
    the irregular income amount in certification period of household_1 is 20.
    q_irregular_income_excluded_from_snap_income expects answers ["the irregular income excluded from snap income of household_1 is 0"].

scenario student_child_earned_income_excluded_at_age_limit is, as stated in "sources/us/statutes/7/2014/d.test.yaml" at case 3:
    person_1 is a person.
    the calculation date is 2026-01-01.
    the child earned income amount of person_1 is 240.
    the person age of person_1 is 17.
    person_1 is child member of household.
    person_1 is elementary or secondary school student.
    q_student_child_earned_income_excluded_from_snap_income expects answers ["the student child earned income excluded from snap income of person_1 is 240"].
    q_student_child_income_age_limit expects answers ["the student child income age limit is 17"].

